{"id": "board-review-line-raised", "title": "Voters raised the line for a public vote on City contracts from $10M to $25M", "seconds": 141.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "3b4e658ef47ccada", "words": 401, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Since 1988, San Francisco has had a rule.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.03, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "pins": [{"place": "cityhall", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "votes on big contracts"}], "zoomOn": "board", "scale": 1.9, "kicker": "San Francisco, since 1988"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.66, 1.5, 1.73, 2.22, 2.35, 2.48, 2.54]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Contracts of 10 million dollars or more need a vote by the Board of Supervisors.", "t0": 3.15, "t1": 7.08, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "pins": [{"place": "cityhall", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "votes on big contracts"}], "zoomOn": "board", "scale": 1.9, "kicker": "San Francisco, since 1988"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.5, 0.6, 0.79, 1.07, 1.4, 1.53, 2.01, 2.22, 2.28, 2.55, 2.69, 2.8, 3.07, 3.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "It’s a check on how contractors perform, and how well the City keeps watch.", "t0": 7.2, "t1": 11.39, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "an opportunity to evaluate contractor performance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.25, 0.53, 0.63, 0.82, 1.43, 2.36, 2.55, 2.71, 3.03, 3.18, 3.46, 3.75]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[4]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "Then, on November 3, 2026,", "t0": 11.51, "t1": 15.3, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "sub": "November 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.62, 0.81, 1.26, 2.05, 2.43]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[4]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "voters passed Proposition E. It raised that line.", "t0": 15.3, "t1": 19.2, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "sub": "November 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.48, 0.91, 1.51, 2.44, 2.67, 3.24, 3.49]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "25 million dollars.", "t0": 19.32, "t1": 20.64, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$25 million", "label": "new line for a Board vote", "sub": "up from $10 million"}, "emph": ["25"], "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 0.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[2]"], "text": "So what slips out of view?", "t0": 21.16, "t1": 23.44, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "the Board’s own research office"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.44, 0.76, 0.9, 0.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[2]"], "text": "The Board’s research office checked 2023 to 2025.", "t0": 23.44, "t1": 27.56, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "the Board’s own research office"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.58, 0.99, 1.29, 1.59, 1.92, 2.81, 2.97, 3.31]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[6]"], "text": "About 2.5 billion dollars.", "t0": 27.68, "t1": 29.42, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2.5 billion", "label": "would have skipped Board review, 2023 to 2025"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.45, 0.69, 0.95, 1.29]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "First, the official record. Proposition E changed the charter, the City’s constitution.", "t0": 30.04, "t1": 35.73, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Three charter amendments", "sub": "proposed by Mayor Daniel Lurie, on the ballot by voter petition"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.73, 0.88, 1.25, 2.15, 2.89, 3.28, 3.66, 3.78, 4.46, 4.61, 4.95]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[0]"], "text": "Before, any change of 500,000 dollars to a big contract got a vote.", "t0": 35.85, "t1": 40.11, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["changes reviewed before", "$500,000 or more"], "b": ["changes reviewed now", "50 percent or more"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.89, 1.17, 1.53, 1.62, 1.83, 2.07, 2.43, 2.73, 2.84, 2.93, 3.17, 3.69, 3.86, 3.93]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[0]"], "text": "Now, only if it adds 50 percent or more.", "t0": 40.23, "t1": 42.22, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["changes reviewed before", "$500,000 or more"], "b": ["changes reviewed now", "50 percent or more"]}, "emph": ["50 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.56, 0.67, 0.75, 1.01, 1.3, 1.59, 1.68]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[10]"], "text": "It passed with 63.76 percent.", "t0": 42.34, "t1": 44.99, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["yes", "207,405"], "b": ["no", "117,874"], "mid": "backed by Lurie, Pelosi, Mandelman and Firefighters Local 798"}, "emph": ["63.76 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 0.64, 1.28, 1.56, 1.89, 2.17]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[11]", "story[3]"], "text": "Two committees named for the Mayor raised 13.07 million dollars.", "t0": 45.11, "t1": 49.31, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Raised by two committees named for the Mayor", "rows": [["Committee one", "$7,635,000"], ["Committee two", "$5,431,550"]]}, "emph": ["13.07 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.64, 0.85, 0.96, 1.08, 1.74, 2.06, 2.57, 2.83, 3.18, 3.45, 3.74]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[12]", "story[4]"], "text": "On November 10, the Mayor announced the first rules under it.", "t0": 49.43, "t1": 52.35, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A purchasing ethics chapter", "sub": "announced November 10, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.54, 1.14, 1.29, 1.57, 1.93, 2.02, 2.32, 2.63, 2.85]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Now the leads. These are questions, not findings by any authority.", "t0": 52.57, "t1": 56.44, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Now, the leads", "sub": "not official findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.33, 1.5, 1.73, 1.88, 2.4, 2.59, 3.04, 3.2, 3.35]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "The first lead: contracts from 10 to 25 million dollars lose their vote.", "t0": 56.56, "t1": 61.66, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "No vote between $10 million and $25 million", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 1.08, 1.61, 1.79, 2.12, 2.21, 2.71, 3.04, 3.91, 4.57, 4.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[6]"], "text": "The second lead: from 2023 to 2025, the Board reviewed 304 contracts.", "t0": 61.88, "t1": 68.32, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "304 contracts reviewed", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2023 to 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.52, 1.3, 1.5, 1.8, 2.42, 2.56, 2.83, 4.07, 4.2, 4.48, 4.9, 5.24, 5.59, 5.84]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[6]"], "text": "Under the new rules, how many?", "t0": 68.44, "t1": 70.38, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "304 contracts reviewed", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2023 to 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.32, 0.49, 0.91, 1.08]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[6]"], "text": "115.", "t0": 70.38, "t1": 71.49, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "115", "label": "contracts reviewed under the new rules", "sub": "189 fewer"}, "emph": ["115"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.53]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "So 189 contracts, about three in five, leave public view.", "t0": 72.01, "t1": 76.67, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["contracts out of view", "189"], "b": ["dollars a year", "$830 million"]}, "emph": ["three in five"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.41, 0.76, 1.23, 2.14, 2.42, 2.68, 2.81, 3.73, 3.99, 4.32]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[7]"], "text": "The third lead: nothing replaces the vote.", "t0": 76.89, "t1": 79.53, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No new oversight or audit mechanism is proposed in the amendments."}, "emph": ["nothing"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.48, 1.18, 1.61, 2.18, 2.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "So under 25 million dollars, only each department’s own checks remain.", "t0": 79.65, "t1": 84.05, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Each department’s own checks", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "for contracts under $25 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.37, 0.94, 1.31, 2.2, 2.51, 2.82, 3.32, 3.55, 3.93]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[8]"], "text": "The fourth lead: three times the Board’s review changed the outcome.", "t0": 84.27, "t1": 87.99, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Three times the vote mattered", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "Files 24-0994, 23-1247 and 23-0692"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.48, 1.2, 1.56, 1.99, 2.08, 2.36, 2.79, 3.15, 3.27]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The Board cut one raise for the Mid-Market Foundation.", "t0": 88.11, "t1": 91.11, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mid-Market Foundation raise, asked", "$7.7 million"], "b": ["after Board review", "$3.8 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.58, 0.84, 1.13, 1.53, 1.65, 1.78, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "From 7.7 million dollars to 3.8 million.", "t0": 91.23, "t1": 95.01, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mid-Market Foundation raise, asked", "$7.7 million"], "b": ["after Board review", "$3.8 million"]}, "emph": ["3.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.62, 0.91, 1.19, 1.47, 2.2, 2.38, 2.69, 3.02, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[2]"], "text": "For the Japanese Community Youth Council, the Board asked for an audit.", "t0": 95.13, "t1": 98.83, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "chip": "$5.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.25, 0.72, 1.16, 1.39, 2.19, 2.33, 2.72, 3.16, 3.29, 3.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[2]"], "text": "It found 5.6 million dollars paid without checking who qualified.", "t0": 98.95, "t1": 102.97, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "chip": "$5.6 million"}, "emph": ["5.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.43, 0.72, 0.99, 1.34, 1.7, 2.03, 2.63, 2.96, 3.28, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Under the new lines, none of the three would have been heard.", "t0": 103.09, "t1": 105.51, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "None would be heard now", "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.29, 0.46, 0.98, 1.18, 1.25, 1.36, 1.65, 1.81, 1.91, 2.07]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The fifth lead: one office now proposes the buying rules.", "t0": 105.73, "t1": 109.06, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "One office writes the buying rules", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "the City Administrator"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.44, 1.27, 1.51, 1.87, 2.12, 2.63, 2.72, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The City Administrator, picked by the Mayor. How much spending do they cover each year?", "t0": 109.18, "t1": 114.33, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "One office writes the buying rules", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "the City Administrator"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.33, 1.2, 1.44, 1.56, 1.66, 2.71, 2.9, 3.1, 3.53, 3.64, 3.77, 4.04, 4.21]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "established[3]"], "text": "More than 6 billion dollars.", "t0": 114.33, "t1": 116.03, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$6 billion", "label": "City contract spending a year"}, "emph": ["More"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.46, 0.85, 1.2]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "The Board can reject a rule within 60 days, but it can’t change a word.", "t0": 116.55, "t1": 120.75, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Reject it whole, or not at all", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "60 days; no amendments"}, "emph": ["change a word"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.57, 0.9, 0.99, 1.26, 1.57, 1.95, 2.9, 3.07, 3.16, 3.46, 3.76, 3.83]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show any contract has skipped review yet.", "t0": 120.97, "t1": 123.64, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any contract has skipped review yet", "That any donor holds a City contract"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.52, 0.74, 0.96, 1.13, 1.6, 1.73, 2.04, 2.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Or that any donor holds a City contract.", "t0": 123.76, "t1": 125.69, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any contract has skipped review yet", "That any donor holds a City contract"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.25, 0.45, 0.79, 1.13, 1.21, 1.44]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The certified results, due by December 3.", "t0": 125.81, "t1": 130.31, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Certified results, due by December 3, 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Contracts of $10 million to $25 million signed after the change"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.46, 0.79, 1.45, 1.64, 2.24, 3.29, 3.51, 3.66, 4.11]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "And a list of contracts in that range signed after the change.", "t0": 130.43, "t1": 133.29, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Certified results, due by December 3, 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Contracts of $10 million to $25 million signed after the change"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.2, 0.4, 0.5, 0.98, 1.08, 1.25, 1.6, 2.02, 2.24, 2.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Proposition E is passing. It’s a change in the rules, not an accusation against anyone.", "t0": 133.41, "t1": 138.68, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.61, 0.91, 1.09, 2.09, 2.29, 2.35, 2.66, 2.75, 2.84, 3.76, 3.95, 4.04, 4.57, 4.87]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 138.8, "t1": 141.01, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.77, 0.92, 1.18, 1.24, 1.33, 1.55, 1.8]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · no vote", "lead2": "Lead 2 · 304 to 115", "lead3": "Lead 3 · nothing in its place", "lead4": "Lead 4 · three that mattered", "lead5": "Lead 5 · one office writes the rules", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "document"}